# Options of rynas-web, read by rynas-web.service (EnvironmentFile).
# Apply changes with: systemctl restart rynas-web

# HTTPS address of the web interface: the door that always works, never behind
# a reverse proxy. [::]:8443 listens on IPv4 and IPv6 (IPv4 only when the
# kernel has no IPv6). The certificate comes from rynas's own local CA
# (/etc/rynas/tls/ui.crt, made and renewed by rynasd; import your own from the
# web interface or the API). "off" disables HTTPS.
RYNAS_WEB_TLS_LISTEN=[::]:8443

# Plain HTTP address. Kept during the transition to HTTPS: once a certificate
# is loaded, requests from other hosts are redirected (307) to
# https://<same host>:8443/; requests from this host (127.0.0.1, ::1: a
# reverse proxy here, an SSH tunnel) are always served as they are.
# 127.0.0.1:8080 closes the plain port to the network entirely.
RYNAS_WEB_LISTEN=0.0.0.0:8080

# Extra command line options, for example:
#   --no-https-redirect         serve plain HTTP to other hosts too
#   --secure-cookies            behind an HTTPS reverse proxy on another host
#   --tls-cert FILE --tls-key FILE
#                               serve another certificate (default: the files
#                               rynasd publishes in /etc/rynas/tls)
#   --admin-group GROUP         who is an administrator (repeatable; replaces
#                               the defaults rynas-admin and sudo)
#   --session-idle-timeout SEC  default 1800
#   --session-max-age SEC       default 43200
# See /usr/libexec/rynas/rynas-web --help
RYNAS_WEB_OPTS=""
